nd is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Peter C. Stern | CEO, President & Director | Age 53 | Compensation: $2.9M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $172K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $90K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Peloton Interactive, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $2.2B market cap on $2.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -4% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -122% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 45%.","The business throws off $378M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 15 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 6.13\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 1.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-1.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (14.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 49% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Piotroski score 8/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Financial quality scores above most Consumer Cyclical peers","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Consumer Cyclical sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 5% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Avoiding Lag: Real-Time Signals in (PTON) Movement","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/91/Avoiding_Lag:_Real-Time_Signals_in_PTON_Movement_111826095202_1795013522.html","date":"2026-11-18","timestamp":1795013522.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.823,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Peloton Interactive, Inc. Announces Successful Completion